{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1322816-what-happens-when-an-angel-fills-its-track-of-bashing-damage","id":1322816,"title":"What happens when an Angel fills its track of Bashing damage?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-07-07T12:13:02-07:00","id":1322816,"title":"What happens when an Angel fills its track of Bashing damage?","content":"<span style=\"color:#242729\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Chronicles of Darkness manual states:</span></span></span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Physical attacks on a Manifested entity that would normally cause lethal damage only cause bashing damage unless the attack utilizes the entity\u2019s bane. Despite appearing to the naked eye and being solid, a Manifested spirit, ghost, or angel doesn\u2019t have any internal organs to injure.</span><br /> </div><span style=\"color:#242729\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">I'm imagining a situation where an angel is taking multiple Lethal attacks each round, which cause only Bashing damage. What happens when the angel's Corpus track fills up with Bashing damage? </span></span></span><ul><li>Do they have to make a reflexive roll to stay conscious?</li> <li>Do the subsequent Lethal attacks then act as Lethal?</li> <li>If that track gets filled again, do they take Aggravated damage?</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#242729\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">I am trying to determine if any attack that does not involve their Bane can stop (even temporarily) an Ephemeral.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T12:51:25-07:00","id":1322819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1322816-what-happens-when-an-angel-fills-its-track-of-bashing-damage#post1322816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do they have to make a reflexive roll to stay conscious?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing objectively says they're immune to this, but it doesn't really make any sense for this to be the case, so I would say no.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do the subsequent Lethal attacks then act as Lethal? </div> </div> </div>This would be the most logical reading of the rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If that track gets filled again, do they take Aggravated damage? </div> </div> </div>Generally not an issue, but yes, wrap around damage would continue to proceed as normal. Ephemeral entities that fill with lethal damage while Manifested immediately discorporate; and the same happens with Aggravated damage anyway (Agg is just more likely to permanently kill them or at least extend their recovery time even longer).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am trying to determine if any attack that does not involve their Bane can stop (even temporarily) an Ephemeral. </div> </div> </div>Yep, it's just a lot harder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T21:59:22-07:00","id":1322886,"title":"","content":"There's a reason why splats who do have inherent edges over their ephemeral foes are big deals, like werewolves. For demons and anything else dealing with angels, part of the point is that <i>nothing</i> really has an edge over them. The host of Heaven are principalities and dominions and thrones given form, not some scrabbling guard of rats or lonely little reality warpers.<br /> <br /> Angels be tough, yo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T03:56:18-07:00","id":1322923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1322816-what-happens-when-an-angel-fills-its-track-of-bashing-damage#post1322816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am trying to determine if any attack that does not involve their Bane can stop (even temporarily) an Ephemeral.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. If you're not able to fill its Corpus twice over to reach full lethal (which is pretty unlikely), you've at least started the process with the first strike. Just keep going at it until you've done enough damage. It's preferable to have buddies around who can help.<br /> If you're asking about whether a single attack does any difference, then no, but that's generally true for everyone unless you use the optional beaten down rules. CofD combat can be dangerously lethal, but only humans going against things out of their league tend to go down in one hit.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you can find some non-Bane means of dealing aggravated damage, such as the Hellfire Exploit for demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}